{"title":"Eliot Bochet-Merand","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Eliot Bochet-Merand","subtitle":"PhD candidate in economics","about":{"template":"trestles","image":"assets/portrait.jpeg","image-shape":"rectangle","image-width":"14em","links":[{"icon":"envelope","text":"Email","href":"mailto:ebochetm@parisnanterre.fr"},{"icon":"file-earmark-text","text":"CV","href":"cv/index.qmd"},{"icon":"github","text":"GitHub","href":"https://github.com/Eliot-bm"}]}},"headingText":"Does automation change who gains from immigration?","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\nAutomation shifts which tasks machines perform. Immigration shifts who performs\nthe rest. They arrive together, and the labour market resolves them jointly ---\nyet we study them apart.\n\nI am a PhD candidate at **Paris Nanterre University**, in the **EconomiX**\nresearch centre, supervised by **Lionel Ragot**. My thesis asks how technical\nchange, human capital and immigration interact in the labour market, using\nFrench administrative data accessed through the CASD.\n\nI came to economics through its philosophy: before this thesis I worked on\nSamuelson's expected utility concept at Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne, and spent a\nyear producing an economics programme for France Culture. Both still shape how I\nchoose questions and how I try to explain answers.\n\n<!-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n     RUBRIQUE \"NEWS\" -- retiree.\n     A remettre uniquement avec des entrees VRAIES. Trois lignes maximum,\n     la plus recente en haut. Un site sans news se lit comme un site jeune ;\n     un site avec de fausses news se lit comme un probleme.\n\n     ## News\n\n     ::: {.news-item}\n     **[Mois annee]** --- [evenement reel].\n     :::\n------------------------------------------------------------------------ -->\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## Does automation change who gains from immigration?\n\nAutomation shifts which tasks machines perform. Immigration shifts who performs\nthe rest. They arrive together, and the labour market resolves them jointly ---\nyet we study them apart.\n\nI am a PhD candidate at **Paris Nanterre University**, in the **EconomiX**\nresearch centre, supervised by **Lionel Ragot**. My thesis asks how technical\nchange, human capital and immigration interact in the labour market, using\nFrench administrative data accessed through the CASD.\n\nI came to economics through its philosophy: before this thesis I worked on\nSamuelson's expected utility concept at Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne, and spent a\nyear producing an economics programme for France Culture. Both still shape how I\nchoose questions and how I try to explain answers.\n\n<!-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n     RUBRIQUE \"NEWS\" -- retiree.\n     A remettre uniquement avec des entrees VRAIES. Trois lignes maximum,\n     la plus recente en haut. Un site sans news se lit comme un site jeune ;\n     un site avec de fausses news se lit comme un probleme.\n\n     ## News\n\n     ::: {.news-item}\n     **[Mois annee]** --- [evenement reel].\n     :::\n------------------------------------------------------------------------ -->\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":"auto","echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-t